\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
For every finite rational metric and $2\leq k<n$, is there one randomized online bit algorithm with polynomial preprocessing in input length L and polynomial work per request in L+log(t+1), guaranteeing expected cost $\leq C(\log (k+1))^{2}OPT+B$ for every finite oblivious sequence, without knowing its horizon?

\subsection{Short English statement}
For every finite rational metric and $2\leq k<n$, is there one randomized online bit algorithm with polynomial preprocessing in input length L and polynomial work per request in L+log(t+1), guaranteeing expected cost $\leq C(\log (k+1))^{2}OPT+B$ for every finite oblivious sequence, without knowing its horizon?

\subsection{Sources}
\begin{itemize}
\item[S1] Original question source or mathematical context.
\url{https://arxiv.org/abs/2205.08103}.
\item[S2] OpenAI, manuscript citation page. Source of the formulation motivating this local problem.
